1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,117
We will move through Earth's horizon.

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:06,257
We will find infinity for sure.

3
00:00:06,340 --> 00:00:13,137
Let's fight for this blue sea and
let the wind take us far away.

4
00:00:13,220 --> 00:00:20,097
Don't give up.

5
00:00:20,180 --> 00:00:22,937
So I can come back to this moment.

6
00:00:23,020 --> 00:00:26,077
So I can be present right here.

7
00:00:26,160 --> 00:00:28,697
Throw away this drop.

8
00:00:28,780 --> 00:00:30,177
Sometimes we share.

9
00:00:30,260 --> 00:00:31,257
Shut it up.

10
00:00:31,340 --> 00:00:34,237
Do not be so afraid to podcast.

11
00:00:34,320 --> 00:00:36,937
To have a friend right here.

12
00:00:37,020 --> 00:00:40,317
And I will always be here by your side.

13
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:42,900
To take care of you.

14
00:00:43,720 --> 00:00:46,297
Even in the darkest of times.

15
00:00:46,380 --> 00:00:47,217
I'll try.

16
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:48,837
Look and breathe it out.

17
00:00:48,920 --> 00:00:50,297
It's alright now.

18
00:00:50,380 --> 00:00:54,017
Cause we are the ones who
are meant to move them up.

19
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:56,737
We will move to our single horizon.

20
00:00:56,820 --> 00:00:59,837
We will find insanity for sure.

21
00:00:59,920 --> 00:01:02,537
We're a world for our heads.

22
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:04,457
We will win for sure.

23
00:01:04,540 --> 00:01:05,497
Dreaming on.

24
00:01:05,580 --> 00:01:07,937
We will move towards the horizon.

25
00:01:08,020 --> 00:01:10,857
We will fight however we can.

26
00:01:10,940 --> 00:01:13,757
In order to be the best we will run.

27
00:01:13,840 --> 00:01:16,477
To the top, to the end.

28
00:01:16,560 --> 00:01:22,180
We gotta be the ones that
just keep dreaming on.

29
00:01:23,100 --> 00:01:25,377
I just can't give up now.

30
00:01:25,460 --> 00:01:28,380
I can never stop cause.

31
00:01:28,880 --> 00:01:31,617
I gotta give everything I got to.

32
00:01:31,700 --> 00:01:35,420
Become the greatest of all times.

33
00:01:36,220 --> 00:01:39,117
We will move towards the horizon.

34
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:41,877
We will find infinite portions.

35
00:01:41,960 --> 00:01:46,717
We will step up and we
will leave for sure.

36
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:48,980
So keep moving on.

37
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:09,020
All right, we'll leave it to you.

38
00:02:09,260 --> 00:02:10,280
Please stay safe.

39
00:02:10,540 --> 00:02:12,280
Do not worry on my behalf.

40
00:02:13,740 --> 00:02:15,420
I give you my word.

41
00:02:15,640 --> 00:02:19,720
I will take Lord Yasui and
return him to where he belongs.

42
00:02:19,980 --> 00:02:23,060
He will be honorably laterest in Kuri.

43
00:02:32,520 --> 00:02:34,080
Have a safe journey!

44
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:37,160
We are so grateful.

45
00:02:37,460 --> 00:02:38,360
Thank you, sir.

46
00:02:38,780 --> 00:02:40,500
It will be my pleasure.

47
00:02:41,100 --> 00:02:45,677
This is the least that I can do to repay
the sacrifice he made for our cause,

48
00:02:45,760 --> 00:02:46,590
after all.

49
00:02:49,140 --> 00:02:50,360
We're all set.

50
00:02:50,820 --> 00:02:52,220
Let's book it, Nami.

51
00:02:52,880 --> 00:02:54,260
Kanjuro! Okay.

52
00:02:54,940 --> 00:02:56,340
Yes, just a moment.

53
00:02:56,580 --> 00:02:58,240
I'll be right with you.

54
00:03:01,140 --> 00:03:02,440
Best of luck.

55
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:04,200
Safe travels to you.

56
00:03:09,760 --> 00:03:13,397
Meanwhile, at a harbor between
the flower capital and Kuri...

57
00:03:13,480 --> 00:03:16,186
The people you see here
are heinous criminals.

58
00:03:16,420 --> 00:03:19,940
They made an attempt on Shogun
Orochi's life, then fled.

59
00:03:20,300 --> 00:03:22,597
We've set up checkpoints
all around the capital.

60
00:03:22,680 --> 00:03:24,327
Line up for your inspection.

61
00:03:29,440 --> 00:03:31,680
Step forward and show your faces.

62
00:03:32,280 --> 00:03:33,460
What should we do?

63
00:03:34,020 --> 00:03:36,017
I had a feeling they might try this.

64
00:03:36,100 --> 00:03:37,806
They wouldn't just let us go.

65
00:03:37,960 --> 00:03:39,980
But there's only one way, Takuri.

66
00:03:40,180 --> 00:03:42,137
We have to take that boat, don't we?

67
00:03:42,220 --> 00:03:45,279
We're gonna need a genius
plan to pull this one off.

68
00:04:07,100 --> 00:04:11,040
A curse upon you!

69
00:04:14,160 --> 00:04:17,860
These poor people are haunted by a ghost!

70
00:04:18,240 --> 00:04:20,640
Here we go, quickly please!

71
00:04:24,680 --> 00:04:26,497
Well, somehow that worked.

72
00:04:26,580 --> 00:04:29,117
How's otoko?

73
00:04:29,200 --> 00:04:33,540
All tuckered out, exhausted
from all that crying. I'm sure.

74
00:04:36,740 --> 00:04:38,217
I feel so bad.

75
00:04:38,300 --> 00:04:40,829
I want to cheer her
up, but what can I say?

76
00:04:41,580 --> 00:04:43,280
Don't leave me!

77
00:04:48,640 --> 00:04:49,820
Please, daddy!

78
00:04:50,800 --> 00:04:53,440
Please, you have to get up!

79
00:05:06,940 --> 00:05:07,770
Bonkichi!

80
00:05:07,853 --> 00:05:09,097
Let me take her!

81
00:05:09,180 --> 00:05:10,417
Your bones are hard!

82
00:05:10,500 --> 00:05:11,780
and likely cold, too.

83
00:05:12,800 --> 00:05:14,020
How dare you?

84
00:05:22,840 --> 00:05:24,500
They're not that cold, guys.

85
00:05:38,720 --> 00:05:39,550
What? What?

86
00:05:39,840 --> 00:05:41,240
It cannot be!

87
00:05:43,620 --> 00:05:45,420
Ships! Ships! Ships!

88
00:05:49,760 --> 00:05:52,840
I have been rendered
speechless. They're splendid.

89
00:05:53,240 --> 00:05:55,828
Save your praise until
after we fix them up.

90
00:05:56,200 --> 00:05:58,837
I pulled them here from
all across the country.

91
00:05:58,920 --> 00:06:01,757
They were left at ports
that Kaido had destroyed.

92
00:06:01,840 --> 00:06:03,697
They'll serve well for the raid.

93
00:06:03,780 --> 00:06:07,486
We'll be able to transport
thousands of warriors to Onigashima.

94
00:06:07,620 --> 00:06:09,660
You're quite dependable after all.

95
00:06:09,900 --> 00:06:12,100
My opinion of you has improved.

96
00:06:12,960 --> 00:06:14,700
Yes, mine has as well.

97
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:17,353
When did you, Gar, get so conscientious?

98
00:06:21,020 --> 00:06:22,196
What did you expect?

99
00:06:22,340 --> 00:06:24,458
You think I just slept for 20 years?

100
00:06:24,580 --> 00:06:27,180
As for the ships, repairs will be easy.

101
00:06:27,540 --> 00:06:29,660
We have Zerfranosuke after all.

102
00:06:30,840 --> 00:06:35,060
This has been a long road, with
many an obstacle along the way.

103
00:06:38,720 --> 00:06:40,000
But I feel it.

104
00:06:40,160 --> 00:06:42,278
Freedom for 1-0 is within our sight.

105
00:07:03,840 --> 00:07:07,697
i thought you took care of big
mom you dipshit do your damn

106
00:07:07,780 --> 00:07:13,340
job i'm quite certain i knocked this
ship off the waterfall, brother.

107
00:07:13,780 --> 00:07:17,340
Why did you bring our enemy here? Shut up!

108
00:07:17,560 --> 00:07:19,442
Our comms were shut off in Udon.

109
00:07:19,660 --> 00:07:21,189
What was I supposed to do?

110
00:07:23,740 --> 00:07:24,570
King!

111
00:07:25,900 --> 00:07:30,000
I'm willing to forgive your
extremely rude attack only

112
00:07:30,640 --> 00:07:31,700
if you join me.

113
00:07:36,540 --> 00:07:39,437
We have all sorts of people
living in my country.

114
00:07:39,520 --> 00:07:42,000
Well, that is to say, all but three.

115
00:07:42,780 --> 00:07:45,440
One of those races is
said to have died out.

116
00:07:45,640 --> 00:07:48,117
So as you might imagine,
they're tough to find.

117
00:07:48,200 --> 00:07:49,940
And yet, here you are.

118
00:07:50,460 --> 00:07:51,440
I refuse.

119
00:07:53,600 --> 00:07:54,430
Hmm.

120
00:07:55,400 --> 00:07:57,140
Ma-ma-ma-ma.

121
00:07:57,700 --> 00:08:00,360
Isn't that a shame? All right?

122
00:08:00,600 --> 00:08:02,797
If you won't join me, uncuff me.

123
00:08:02,880 --> 00:08:04,292
That's not how it works!

124
00:08:04,400 --> 00:08:05,400
Are you crazy?

125
00:08:05,900 --> 00:08:06,940
Hey, you guys.

126
00:08:07,640 --> 00:08:08,470
Huh?

127
00:08:08,553 --> 00:08:09,383
Huh?

128
00:08:09,466 --> 00:08:10,296
Did you know?

129
00:08:10,379 --> 00:08:14,180
Big Mom and Commander Kaido used
to be in the same pirate crew!

130
00:08:14,420 --> 00:08:16,660
Take those cuffs off now, fools.

131
00:08:17,140 --> 00:08:18,964
What do you think you're doing?

132
00:08:21,980 --> 00:08:23,200
Commander Kaido!

133
00:08:23,560 --> 00:08:25,660
You showed up after all, Lin-Win.

134
00:08:26,020 --> 00:08:27,160
It's been a while.

135
00:08:31,280 --> 00:08:32,110
Kaido!

136
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:44,380
Hey, you dopes!

137
00:08:44,680 --> 00:08:47,700
He told you to take these
handcuffs off! What?

138
00:08:48,780 --> 00:08:50,427
I'm sure he was just joking!

139
00:08:50,560 --> 00:08:52,297
That would be completely insane!

140
00:08:52,380 --> 00:08:53,560
Take them off!

141
00:08:53,820 --> 00:08:55,140
If you insist!

142
00:09:04,120 --> 00:09:07,280
Why, it's been decades, hasn't it?

143
00:09:08,320 --> 00:09:09,150
Napoleon!

144
00:09:13,800 --> 00:09:15,260
Right here, Mama!

145
00:09:15,760 --> 00:09:17,000
I'm so happy!

146
00:09:17,200 --> 00:09:18,437
You're back to normal!

147
00:09:18,520 --> 00:09:21,285
I'm shy around strangers,
so I didn't come out!

148
00:09:22,880 --> 00:09:26,320
I said I would kill you if you came here.

149
00:09:26,500 --> 00:09:30,324
If you think I came here to die,
you've got another thing coming!

150
00:09:47,200 --> 00:09:50,280
Oh, my God.

151
00:10:24,520 --> 00:10:29,980
Two-sword style, 7.20 caliber Phoenix!

152
00:10:40,900 --> 00:10:43,520
You think fighting one storm will stop me?

153
00:10:50,040 --> 00:10:51,340
This is ridiculous.

154
00:10:51,740 --> 00:10:53,505
What is the point of all this?

155
00:10:53,720 --> 00:10:56,500
Are you an ally or are you an enemy?

156
00:10:58,540 --> 00:11:00,240
Who the hell are you?

157
00:11:13,220 --> 00:11:14,817
Why do you need all these weapons?

158
00:11:14,900 --> 00:11:15,837
What are you doing?

159
00:11:15,920 --> 00:11:17,557
Waiting on this bridge
in the middle of nowhere?

160
00:11:17,640 --> 00:11:21,617
Just give me back my sword
before I have to cut you,

161
00:11:21,700 --> 00:11:24,197
like you said, one's not a loss for you.

162
00:11:24,280 --> 00:11:26,633
And it's certainly not worth dying over.

163
00:11:40,780 --> 00:11:42,080
Not that sword!

164
00:11:42,400 --> 00:11:44,800
Any other blade I would let you take!

165
00:11:52,880 --> 00:11:55,217
Shusui should have never been taken away!

166
00:11:55,300 --> 00:11:57,888
It's an irreplaceable
treasure to this land!

167
00:12:01,260 --> 00:12:02,090
Shusui?

168
00:12:02,173 --> 00:12:06,177
That was the start of Wano's ruin
when this country lost Shusui!

169
00:12:06,260 --> 00:12:09,780
It was a crime that enraged
our God of the Blade.

170
00:12:10,100 --> 00:12:12,660
Each region was attacked one by one.

171
00:12:12,920 --> 00:12:15,560
Then the country was
conquered by the enemy!

172
00:12:19,700 --> 00:12:21,620
He wasn't a god!

173
00:12:23,180 --> 00:12:25,060
Cease your blasphemy!

174
00:12:43,080 --> 00:12:44,840
Stop fighting!

175
00:13:00,320 --> 00:13:03,537
Is this some sort of performance piece?

176
00:13:03,620 --> 00:13:07,502
Why would a samurai and a monk be
fighting each other in the snow?

177
00:13:07,820 --> 00:13:12,055
It seems you're trying to spare each
other's lives rather than end them.

178
00:13:12,240 --> 00:13:13,520
A fish man?

179
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:41,040
He's... alive!

180
00:13:42,040 --> 00:13:44,280
Is that you, Kawamatsu?

181
00:13:46,320 --> 00:13:48,020
How do you know my name?

182
00:13:53,500 --> 00:13:55,560
Those two just keep going at it!

183
00:13:55,760 --> 00:14:00,100
I think we'd better pull back to the
mainland. Hey, you! What the hell?

184
00:14:00,600 --> 00:14:02,637
Your boss is out there kicking ass,

185
00:14:02,720 --> 00:14:06,537
and you guys are in here cowering
and talking about running away?

186
00:14:06,620 --> 00:14:08,620
Okay, but why are you here?

187
00:14:08,800 --> 00:14:11,040
Were you gonna escape, too? Oh?

188
00:14:12,260 --> 00:14:13,090
No.

189
00:14:13,300 --> 00:14:14,720
What gave you that idea?

190
00:14:18,640 --> 00:14:21,477
Uh, anyway, have you gotten
a call from Udon yet?

191
00:14:21,560 --> 00:14:24,913
I'm afraid not, and we can't
reach them by smell, either.

192
00:14:26,960 --> 00:14:27,790
Yes!

193
00:14:27,873 --> 00:14:30,017
I'll go there and check
if everything's okay.

194
00:14:30,100 --> 00:14:31,917
You're just trying to escape from here!

195
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:32,941
That's cheating!

196
00:14:33,300 --> 00:14:34,397
I'll be right back.

197
00:14:34,480 --> 00:14:35,720
I'm just popping in.

198
00:14:39,440 --> 00:14:42,280
Give me that. Yes, sir. Sorry. Click.

199
00:14:44,380 --> 00:14:45,940
What's up? This is Queen.

200
00:14:49,160 --> 00:14:50,800
This is the Chief Warden.

201
00:14:51,020 --> 00:14:52,980
It seems we finally got through.

202
00:14:53,760 --> 00:14:54,590
Good.

203
00:14:54,673 --> 00:14:56,737
That means you fixed the smells, I assume.

204
00:14:56,820 --> 00:14:58,340
Yes, just a moment ago.

205
00:14:58,700 --> 00:15:01,537
Well, as it turns out, I don't
need all these men here after all.

206
00:15:01,620 --> 00:15:04,497
If you're shorthanded, how
about I make a trip back?

207
00:15:04,580 --> 00:15:07,037
That's just another excuse for him to run!

208
00:15:07,120 --> 00:15:09,600
Actually, that won't be necessary. Oh!

209
00:15:10,660 --> 00:15:11,490
Rejected!

210
00:15:11,840 --> 00:15:14,477
All of our enemies are
sitting quietly behind bars.

211
00:15:14,560 --> 00:15:18,637
That includes Straw Hat, Luffy,
Captain Kidd, and all the other rebels.

212
00:15:18,720 --> 00:15:19,660
Is that so?

213
00:15:19,900 --> 00:15:22,177
I just called to let you
know that all is well.

214
00:15:22,260 --> 00:15:23,660
Well, I wish it wasn't!

215
00:15:23,820 --> 00:15:25,232
Now you're being pretty!

216
00:15:27,040 --> 00:15:28,180
That's all from me.

217
00:15:28,440 --> 00:15:29,680
Until next time.

218
00:15:31,240 --> 00:15:33,340
I hope that I please you, my lady.

219
00:15:33,600 --> 00:15:35,640
Did I do good? Mm-hmm.

220
00:15:35,800 --> 00:15:37,180
Yes, that was perfect.

221
00:15:37,600 --> 00:15:38,980
Who's a good boy?

222
00:15:39,340 --> 00:15:40,340
I am.

223
00:15:42,340 --> 00:15:44,220
What splendid sorcery.

224
00:15:44,340 --> 00:15:47,164
She tamed her enemy with
a mere millet dumpling.

225
00:15:48,560 --> 00:15:52,501
She can tame beasts, but also those
who have obtained beast powers.

226
00:15:54,380 --> 00:15:56,968
Looks like everything
worked out in the end.

227
00:15:57,520 --> 00:16:00,660
Hm, thanks to your
efforts, we are grateful.

228
00:16:00,940 --> 00:16:02,660
How kind, but you're right.

229
00:16:02,940 --> 00:16:05,260
I was rather clever, wasn't I?

230
00:16:06,760 --> 00:16:10,701
After I gobbled up their boss snail,
their communications were cut.

231
00:16:11,020 --> 00:16:13,902
That means no pesky
reinforcements for the enemy.

232
00:16:14,940 --> 00:16:16,337
Oh, I can't wait.

233
00:16:16,420 --> 00:16:20,497
On the day of the battle, they'll be
in for an ugly surprise, won't they?

234
00:16:24,740 --> 00:16:27,157
So don't forget my
contributions to your cause.

235
00:16:27,240 --> 00:16:29,257
We're in this together now, you and I.

236
00:16:29,340 --> 00:16:30,877
For that, I'm glad.

237
00:16:30,960 --> 00:16:35,380
Onward, with the smells working, let
us contact Keenemon and the others.

238
00:16:37,700 --> 00:16:39,080
Sa tu Ramen.

239
00:16:40,080 --> 00:16:44,657
I promise, we shall repay this
debt even if it costs us our lives.

240
00:16:44,740 --> 00:16:48,157
It's fine coming, it wasn't
any trouble to beat that virus!

241
00:16:48,240 --> 00:16:52,060
And your Samurai honor thing
is a bit much, so no thank you.

242
00:16:52,560 --> 00:16:54,501
Well, at least it all worked out.

243
00:16:55,120 --> 00:16:56,767
Luffy Tato's back in action.

244
00:16:56,920 --> 00:16:58,800
We got this! You ready?

245
00:16:59,440 --> 00:17:00,270
Yeah!

246
00:17:01,360 --> 00:17:02,190
Luffy Daddy!

247
00:17:02,273 --> 00:17:03,180
You're the man!

248
00:17:04,880 --> 00:17:08,351
And he's kicking a few friends
left and right, like always.

249
00:17:09,040 --> 00:17:11,797
All it took was a little
push from Lord Momonosuke,

250
00:17:11,880 --> 00:17:13,115
and they came around.

251
00:17:14,380 --> 00:17:15,977
I know that face.

252
00:17:16,060 --> 00:17:18,580
Still has that aura about him, doesn't he?

253
00:17:18,840 --> 00:17:20,420
How long has it been?

254
00:17:20,920 --> 00:17:22,980
We missed you, boss Hyogoro.

255
00:17:29,300 --> 00:17:31,420
Oh my, it's them!

256
00:17:32,940 --> 00:17:34,620
Blood-riding Omasa!

257
00:17:36,940 --> 00:17:38,600
Split-hat Tsunaguro!

258
00:17:41,320 --> 00:17:43,020
Hojo the Pottle Gourd!

259
00:17:44,740 --> 00:17:48,417
and snake eyes, yatape
leaders of the underground,

260
00:17:48,500 --> 00:17:50,597
from all across the land, were right here.

261
00:17:50,680 --> 00:17:54,437
This is an honor; I never thought
I'd live to serve you again.

262
00:17:54,520 --> 00:17:57,297
The honor is mine; I'm so glad.

263
00:17:57,380 --> 00:17:58,457
You're alive and well.

264
00:17:58,540 --> 00:18:02,997
We're not worthy of your kindness,
yeah. You've got that. It's backwards.

265
00:18:03,080 --> 00:18:04,857
It's taking a crap after a bath!

266
00:18:04,940 --> 00:18:08,040
Yeah, what he said precisely, so?

267
00:18:10,980 --> 00:18:12,580
What a bunch of weirdos!

268
00:18:12,720 --> 00:18:14,955
These guys' hands are to you, old man?

269
00:18:16,660 --> 00:18:17,540
Old man!

270
00:18:18,240 --> 00:18:19,070
Whoa!

271
00:18:21,720 --> 00:18:22,920
Now tear your nails!

272
00:18:23,040 --> 00:18:23,917
Cover your toes!

273
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:25,220
Rip off your ears!

274
00:18:25,760 --> 00:18:27,780
You'll pay in body parts for that!

275
00:18:27,940 --> 00:18:29,277
What do you want us to take, boss?

276
00:18:29,360 --> 00:18:30,190
And how many?

277
00:18:30,480 --> 00:18:31,780
Just give us the word!

278
00:18:31,900 --> 00:18:33,057
Don't take anything!

279
00:18:33,140 --> 00:18:34,437
That man saved my life!

280
00:18:34,520 --> 00:18:35,873
Put him down right now!

281
00:18:42,320 --> 00:18:43,700
Don't you worry, boss.

282
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:45,117
If there are any rebels left,

283
00:18:45,200 --> 00:18:49,357
we'll find them and bring them to your
side, no matter where they're hiding.

284
00:18:49,440 --> 00:18:51,740
Splendid. Do your best. Yes, sir.

285
00:18:52,800 --> 00:18:55,340
Seems you escaped death, kid. For today.

286
00:18:55,940 --> 00:19:00,340
I hope you learned your lesson for
next time. Shut up! You're lame!

287
00:19:08,660 --> 00:19:09,820
My word!

288
00:19:10,200 --> 00:19:11,320
What a surprise!

289
00:19:11,700 --> 00:19:15,994
To think you were the mystery man from
Kuri who stole Kaido's blueprints!

290
00:19:16,400 --> 00:19:17,230
How fortunate!

291
00:19:17,313 --> 00:19:19,037
Long have we searched for this!

292
00:19:19,120 --> 00:19:21,820
The layout of the mansion on Onigashima!

293
00:19:22,760 --> 00:19:26,320
A shame that I wasted so
much of Surfer Nosuke's time.

294
00:19:27,220 --> 00:19:31,200
But now, we can plan our
attack on enemy territory!

295
00:19:32,340 --> 00:19:34,200
What a reliable ally!

296
00:19:34,740 --> 00:19:37,457
When did Yugar get so conscientious?

297
00:19:37,540 --> 00:19:40,305
Are you gonna keep saying
that every time, dog?

298
00:19:45,740 --> 00:19:48,420
Is that you, Race? What's the word?

299
00:19:48,620 --> 00:19:51,385
Have you managed to rescue
Sir Luffy Daddy yet?

300
00:19:51,860 --> 00:19:54,177
Indeed we have, but that
is only the beginning.

301
00:19:54,260 --> 00:19:58,554
I'll spare you the details for now,
but we just recruited 3,500 warriors.

302
00:20:05,500 --> 00:20:07,400
3,500 warriors?

303
00:20:07,880 --> 00:20:09,440
That's no small number.

304
00:20:09,760 --> 00:20:12,017
So you've not only saved
Sir Luffy as planned,

305
00:20:12,100 --> 00:20:15,041
you've also freed Kawamatsu
and recruited an army?

306
00:20:15,360 --> 00:20:18,220
Hold on, Kawamatsu is
locked in that prison?

307
00:20:18,420 --> 00:20:21,538
You mean the entire region
is under your control now?

308
00:20:21,880 --> 00:20:25,762
You've got to have achieved far
more than a rescue mission, Raizo.

309
00:20:26,280 --> 00:20:27,320
Next stop!

310
00:20:31,860 --> 00:20:34,897
Our friends are recruiting
even more allies as we speak,

311
00:20:34,980 --> 00:20:38,517
however, with that comes a
complication which we must address.

312
00:20:38,600 --> 00:20:43,157
This land has several weapons
factories, as you surely know,

313
00:20:43,240 --> 00:20:45,677
but their products are intended for export

314
00:20:45,760 --> 00:20:47,817
and do not stay in the
land of Wano for long.

315
00:20:47,900 --> 00:20:50,437
Since our forces are mostly samurai,

316
00:20:50,520 --> 00:20:55,237
they are skilled with swords and
spears, but as you can imagine,

317
00:20:55,320 --> 00:20:57,697
those are difficult to
come by since Orochi

318
00:20:57,780 --> 00:20:59,757
has banned citizens from carrying weapons,

319
00:20:59,840 --> 00:21:02,037
no matter how many allies we have,

320
00:21:02,120 --> 00:21:05,197
if they are not properly armed,
our plan is doomed to fail!

321
00:21:05,280 --> 00:21:10,057
Very well, I understand
this is a serious matter.

322
00:21:10,140 --> 00:21:11,457
What to do?

323
00:21:11,540 --> 00:21:18,197
I shall give this

324
00:21:18,280 --> 00:21:19,110
quandary some thought,

325
00:21:19,193 --> 00:21:20,277
but I must go.

326
00:21:20,360 --> 00:21:21,377
I'll inform.

327
00:21:21,460 --> 00:21:23,397
of our group's accomplishments later.

328
00:21:23,480 --> 00:21:28,186
For the time being, I will head to Amagasa
Village and gauge their preparedness.

329
00:21:29,080 --> 00:21:32,757
Race, I look forward to sharing the
details of our mutual victories.

330
00:21:32,840 --> 00:21:33,720
As do I.

331
00:21:34,280 --> 00:21:35,110
Click.

332
00:21:40,720 --> 00:21:42,460
And now, we depart.

333
00:21:47,680 --> 00:21:52,580
I can scarcely believe my eyes,
But I'd know that face anywhere.

334
00:21:54,040 --> 00:21:54,940
Kawamatsu!

335
00:22:03,400 --> 00:22:05,020
It can't be.

336
00:22:05,500 --> 00:22:08,080
Is that really you?

337
00:22:13,120 --> 00:22:14,020
Kawamatsu!

338
00:22:33,680 --> 00:22:37,460
It is you, to think I would
find you in a place like this.

339
00:22:38,280 --> 00:22:41,437
But never mind, if you are
well, that's all that matters.

340
00:22:41,520 --> 00:22:43,980
My heart leaps with joy to find you safe.

341
00:22:44,980 --> 00:22:45,940
Lady Hiyori.

342
00:22:48,080 --> 00:22:49,420
Oh yeah, that's right.

343
00:22:50,180 --> 00:22:53,757
She said something about being raised
by a cop after her parents died.

344
00:22:53,840 --> 00:22:54,840
Forgive me.

345
00:22:55,240 --> 00:22:58,960
Back then, I only ran away
because I feared for your health.

346
00:23:00,220 --> 00:23:04,867
Even if it was only a scrap, you always
gave me every morsel of food you found.

347
00:23:11,800 --> 00:23:14,680
It appears that I am still
lacking as a samurai.

348
00:23:20,060 --> 00:23:20,890
Kawamatsu!

349
00:23:21,360 --> 00:23:24,300
I couldn't stand to watch you waste away,

350
00:23:25,040 --> 00:23:28,637
especially knowing that you could
easily survive if you were alone.

351
00:23:28,720 --> 00:23:32,367
I couldn't stand the thought
that you might die because of me.

352
00:23:55,400 --> 00:24:01,660
I'm sorry for leaving you, Kawamatsu, but
if nothing is done, I fear you may die.

353
00:24:03,880 --> 00:24:07,900
It was painful, but what could I do?

354
00:24:12,060 --> 00:24:16,217
Dear Kawamatsu, thank you for everything.

355
00:24:16,300 --> 00:24:17,660
I'll be fine, Hiyori.

356
00:24:19,360 --> 00:24:20,437
Lady...

357
00:24:20,520 --> 00:24:22,360
Lady Hiyori!

358
00:24:28,200 --> 00:24:30,520
Lady Hiyori!

359
00:24:32,240 --> 00:24:33,360
Your Majesty!

360
00:24:37,660 --> 00:24:39,080
Would you believe it?

361
00:24:39,200 --> 00:24:41,376
I washed my hair all by myself today!

362
00:24:41,560 --> 00:24:43,560
All I had to do was close my eyes!

363
00:24:43,800 --> 00:24:44,920
Not here.

364
00:24:46,620 --> 00:24:47,840
Where to next?

365
00:24:56,560 --> 00:24:57,680
Lady Hiyori!

366
00:25:07,220 --> 00:25:09,980
Oh, Lady Hiyori, why'd you run away?

367
00:25:29,160 --> 00:25:31,840
My lady, please.

368
00:25:41,880 --> 00:25:43,840
Where did you go?

369
00:25:45,640 --> 00:25:48,760
What have I done wrong, my lady?

370
00:25:49,440 --> 00:25:50,270
Why?

371
00:25:56,520 --> 00:25:58,500
Come back.

372
00:25:59,060 --> 00:26:01,140
Lady Hiyori!

373
00:26:07,580 --> 00:26:09,560
I'm so sorry.

374
00:26:10,380 --> 00:26:11,960
You must have suffered.

375
00:26:12,740 --> 00:26:15,200
Now I finally know why you ran away.

376
00:26:15,720 --> 00:26:17,660
How kind of you to think of me.

377
00:26:17,880 --> 00:26:21,056
Though thanks to that, I put
on quite a lot of weight.

378
00:26:31,520 --> 00:26:32,980
Who goes there?

379
00:26:36,500 --> 00:26:38,577
Your days are numbered, Kikimari!

380
00:26:38,660 --> 00:26:42,097
You really think you could steal
our weapons and get away with it?

381
00:26:42,180 --> 00:26:44,945
I'll take them back along
with everything else!

382
00:26:48,660 --> 00:26:50,160
These are hunting rounds.

383
00:26:50,460 --> 00:26:52,695
They take down things twice your size!

384
00:26:54,140 --> 00:26:55,897
Hide behind that tree, my lady.

385
00:26:55,980 --> 00:26:56,810
I shall.

386
00:26:58,360 --> 00:26:59,190
Huh?

387
00:26:59,273 --> 00:27:00,257
Are those buddies of his?

388
00:27:00,340 --> 00:27:01,397
What does it matter?

389
00:27:01,480 --> 00:27:03,186
Just shoot them all to death!

390
00:27:04,640 --> 00:27:05,680
Go to hell!

391
00:27:13,140 --> 00:27:14,100
Oh, oh!

392
00:27:14,580 --> 00:27:15,600
Kappa style!

393
00:27:15,800 --> 00:27:16,900
Two-sword style!

394
00:27:17,160 --> 00:27:18,460
River of Retribution!

395
00:27:18,660 --> 00:27:19,580
Rhino cycle!

396
00:27:21,120 --> 00:27:32,130
Ah!

397
00:27:32,213 --> 00:27:33,043
Ah! Ah! Ah!

398
00:27:33,126 --> 00:27:33,956
Shikawa Matsu!

399
00:27:35,020 --> 00:27:35,850
Ah!

400
00:27:36,000 --> 00:27:37,297
Are you all right?

401
00:27:37,380 --> 00:27:39,560
As long as you are, Lady Hiyori.

402
00:27:41,880 --> 00:27:44,480
I can't believe it's you!

403
00:27:48,380 --> 00:27:49,321
Hey, wait a sec!

404
00:27:49,540 --> 00:27:51,128
Are you running away again?

405
00:27:51,880 --> 00:27:52,710
Asshole!

406
00:27:52,793 --> 00:27:54,300
Give me my sword!

407
00:27:59,560 --> 00:28:00,800
Shikawa Matsu!

408
00:28:01,020 --> 00:28:02,280
It's really you!

409
00:28:02,480 --> 00:28:04,120
I'm so glad you're alive!

410
00:28:08,180 --> 00:28:09,540
Thank you.
